### 4.3 Good Track Selection

The TPC readout consists of 45 pad-rows where hits may be measured. The more hits in the TPC that are found and used the better the track may be described to discern it momentum and energy loss. However, requiring many hits in the TPC means that many tracks will be rejected and the tracking efficiency and detector acceptance will be reduced. Then the corrections for these effects will be larger and the sensitivity of the measurement to how well we can model detector effects on track reconstruction is increased. For this analysis, a minimum of 15 space charge points in the TPC are required for each track. This cuts out \(\approx\) 2% of the tracks. Also, in order to prevent the splitting of hits from a single track into two or more tracks, a cut is included that requires that the number of hits used in the fit divided by the number of possible hits for a track of that geometry is greater than 0.52. This cut removes \(<\) 1% of tracks.

