### 5.3 Identified Spectra Fits

The charged hadron efficiency is constructed as the weighted average of the single species efficiencies where the weights are provided by fits to the corrected spectra using Eq. 5.5,

\[spectra=\frac{1}{2\pi p_{\rm T}}\frac{d^{2}N_{i}^{j}}{d\eta dp_{\rm T}}(p_{\rm T} )={\rm p0}\cdot(1-{\rm p1}(1-{\rm p2})\cdot p_{\rm T}^{2})^{\frac{1}{1-{\rm p2 }}}, \tag{5.5}\]

