Fully corrected charged hadron \(p_{\rm T}\)-spectra measured in \(|\eta|<0.5\) are shown in Fig. 7.1. The spectra are shown for 0-5%, 5-10%, 10-20%, 20-40%, 40-60%, and 60-80% centralities in \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{\rm NN}}}=7.7\), 11.5, 14.5, 19.6, 27, 39, and 62.4 GeV collisions. The \(p_{\rm T}\) reach generally increases for more central spectra, except in a few cases where theFigure 7.1: Corrected charged hadron spectra for each \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{\mathrm{NN}}}}\) and centrality bin as a function of \(p_{\mathrm{T}}\) and measured in \(|\eta|<0.5\). Systematic uncertainty bands are shown but are generally smaller than the symbol size.

narrower centrality bins of the most central spectra result in fewer measured tracks and a reduced \(p_{\rm T}\) reach. The spectra fall more steeply for lower \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{\rm NN}}}\) and there is also a strong centrality dependence to the slopes at lower \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{\rm NN}}}\). Systematic uncertainties from the feed-down, momentum resolution, and tracking efficiency corrections are included in Fig. 7.1, but are generally too small to be seen.

